import Mathlib
import IUT.PaperIV.Proposition1_5

/-!
# IUT IV, Proposition 1.5 (i) and (ii) on the tensor product `ℂ ⊗_ℝ ℂ`

Source: Mochizuki, *Inter-universal Teichmüller Theory IV*, Proposition 1.5 (archimedean
metric estimates) and its proof, pages 14 to 16. Pages read for this file: 14, 15 and 16; all
three were checked against rendered images, including every formula used below.

This file is not a formalization of the whole of Proposition 1.5. It proves assertions (i)
and (ii) in full on the objects of the page, together with the bracketed claim that the
primitive automorphisms form a group of order `8`. Assertions (iii) and (iv) are not proved
here; see "Not proved" below. The module `IUT.PaperIV.Proposition1_5` checks the same factor `2`
in coordinates and the count `2^{|I|-1}·|V|^{|I|}`; this file works on the tensor product
itself.

## Objects

* `ℂ` carries its standard Hermitian metric, read as the real inner product
  `⟪z, w⟫ = Re(z·w̄)` of Mathlib (`ℂ` as a real inner product space).
* `ℂ ⊗_ℝ ℂ` is Mathlib's `TensorProduct ℝ ℂ ℂ` with its `ℝ`-algebra structure and Mathlib's
  tensor product inner product (`⟪a ⊗ b, c ⊗ d⟫ = ⟪a, c⟫·⟪b, d⟫`); its topology is the one of
  that norm.
* `ℂ ⊕ ℂ` is the ring `ℂ × ℂ`; its direct sum metric is `archDsInner`, the sum of the inner
  products of the components.
* The primitive automorphisms (`archPrimitive`) are the subgroup of the group `ℂ ≃ₗᵢ[ℝ] ℂ`
  of automorphisms of the metrized real vector space `ℂ` generated by complex conjugation and
  multiplication by `±1`, `±√−1`, as printed on page 14.
* The automorphism of `ℂ ⊗_ℝ ℂ` induced by primitive automorphisms `f`, `g` of the two copies
  of `ℂ` is `f ⊗ g` (`TensorProduct.congrIsometry f g`).

## Readings of the page

* "Isomorphism of topological rings" is read as a ring isomorphism
  `ℂ ⊗_ℝ ℂ ≅ ℂ × ℂ` that is continuous. The theorems quantify over all of them; one example
  is `archCrt`, `a ⊗ b ↦ (a·b, a·b̄)`, which is continuous (`archCrt_continuous`).
* "The metric on the right-hand side corresponds to 2 times the metric on the left-hand side"
  is read as the identity of inner products `⟪φ x, φ y⟫ = 2·⟪x, y⟫`; the bracketed form,
  lengths differ by `√2`, is a separate theorem.
* "The direct sum decomposition, together with its Hermitian metric, is preserved" is read
  as: the induced map of `ℂ ⊕ ℂ` preserves the direct sum metric and maps each of the two
  summands onto a summand (`archPermutesSummands`). It cannot mean that each summand is
  mapped onto itself: conjugation on one factor exchanges the two summands.

## Main results

* `archProp1_5_i`: for every continuous ring isomorphism `φ : ℂ ⊗_ℝ ℂ ≅ ℂ ⊕ ℂ`,
  `archDsInner (φ x) (φ y) = 2 * ⟪x, y⟫`.
* `archProp1_5_i_length`: `√(‖(φ x)₁‖² + ‖(φ x)₂‖²) = √2 · ‖x‖`.
* `archPrimitive_card`: the group of primitive automorphisms has order `8`.
* `archProp1_5_ii`: for every such `φ` and primitive `f`, `g`, the map
  `z ↦ φ((f ⊗ g)(φ⁻¹ z))` preserves the direct sum metric and the two summands.

Steps: `archCrt` is an `ℝ`-algebra isomorphism (surjective, and both sides have real dimension
`4`) with `archCrt_inner`; a continuous ring isomorphism is `ℝ`-linear
(`archAlgEquivOfContinuous`), so it is `archCrt` followed by an `ℝ`-algebra automorphism of
`ℂ × ℂ`, and every such automorphism is `(g₁, g₂)` or `(g₁, g₂)` after the swap with
`gᵢ ∈ {id, conj}` (`archAut_form`), hence an isometry that preserves the summands. Every
primitive automorphism is `z ↦ u·z` or `z ↦ u·z̄` with `u⁴ = 1` (`archPrimitive_form`), and
`f ⊗ g` corresponds under `archCrt` to an explicit map (`archInducedForm_crt`).

## Not proved

* Assertion (iii): the topological ring structure on `M_I = ⊗_{i ∈ I} M_i`, its unique
  decomposition as a direct sum of `2^{|I|-1}·|V|^{|I|}` copies of `ℂ`, the equality of the
  direct sum metric with `2^{|I|-1}` times the tensor product metric, the integral structure
  `B_I` and its preservation by the automorphisms induced by primitive automorphisms. The
  obstacle is the library: Mathlib has an inner product on binary tensor products only, not
  on the tensor product `PiTensorProduct` of a family indexed by a finite set `I` (only the
  projective and injective seminorms, which are other norms), and it has no decomposition of
  `⊗_{i ∈ I} (V → ℂ)` over `ℝ` into copies of `ℂ`. Building these is a separate piece of work;
  no weaker statement is given under the name of (iii) here. `IUT.PaperIV.Proposition1_5Many`
  defines a tensor product metric on `M_I` (`tmetForm`) and checks (iii) for it; that metric is
  not identified, for two factors, with the inner product used in this file.
* Assertion (iv), here; it is checked for that metric in `IUT.PaperIV.Proposition1_5Many`
  (`tmetProp1_5_iv`).
* The proof on page 16 refers to IUT III, Remark 3.9.1 (ii); the arguments here are direct
  and do not formalize that remark.

The page does not define a log-volume in Proposition 1.5; no log-volume appears here.
-/

namespace IUT.PaperIV.Proposition1_5

open Complex ComplexConjugate

/-! ## The direct sum metric and the two summands of `ℂ ⊕ ℂ` -/

/-- The direct sum metric on `ℂ ⊕ ℂ` (written `ℂ × ℂ`): the sum of the real inner products
`⟪z, w⟫ = Re(z·w̄)` of the two components, each copy of `ℂ` carrying its standard Hermitian
metric. -/
noncomputable def archDsInner (x y : ℂ × ℂ) : ℝ :=
  inner ℝ x.1 y.1 + inner ℝ x.2 y.2

/-- The summand `ℂ ⊕ 0` of `ℂ ⊕ ℂ`. -/
def archSummandFst : Set (ℂ × ℂ) := {z | z.2 = 0}

/-- The summand `0 ⊕ ℂ` of `ℂ ⊕ ℂ`. -/
def archSummandSnd : Set (ℂ × ℂ) := {z | z.1 = 0}

/-- A map `T` of `ℂ ⊕ ℂ` preserves the direct sum decomposition: it maps each of the two
summands onto a summand (both onto themselves, or each onto the other). -/
def archPermutesSummands (T : ℂ × ℂ → ℂ × ℂ) : Prop :=
  (T '' archSummandFst = archSummandFst ∧ T '' archSummandSnd = archSummandSnd) ∨
    (T '' archSummandFst = archSummandSnd ∧ T '' archSummandSnd = archSummandFst)

theorem archDsInner_add_left (x x' y : ℂ × ℂ) :
    archDsInner (x + x') y = archDsInner x y + archDsInner x' y := by
  simp only [archDsInner, Prod.fst_add, Prod.snd_add, inner_add_left]; ring

theorem archDsInner_add_right (x y y' : ℂ × ℂ) :
    archDsInner x (y + y') = archDsInner x y + archDsInner x y' := by
  simp only [archDsInner, Prod.fst_add, Prod.snd_add, inner_add_right]; ring

theorem archDsInner_zero_left (y : ℂ × ℂ) : archDsInner 0 y = 0 := by
  simp [archDsInner]

theorem archDsInner_zero_right (x : ℂ × ℂ) : archDsInner x 0 = 0 := by
  simp [archDsInner]

/-- The direct sum metric on the diagonal is the sum of the squared lengths. -/
theorem archDsInner_self (x : ℂ × ℂ) : archDsInner x x = ‖x.1‖ ^ 2 + ‖x.2‖ ^ 2 := by
  simp only [archDsInner, real_inner_self_eq_norm_sq]

/-- Composition of maps that preserve the decomposition preserves it. -/
theorem archPermutesSummands_comp {T T' : ℂ × ℂ → ℂ × ℂ} (hT : archPermutesSummands T)
    (hT' : archPermutesSummands T') : archPermutesSummands (T ∘ T') := by
  unfold archPermutesSummands at *
  simp only [Set.image_comp]
  rcases hT with ⟨h1, h2⟩ | ⟨h1, h2⟩ <;> rcases hT' with ⟨h1', h2'⟩ | ⟨h1', h2'⟩ <;>
    simp [h1, h2, h1', h2']

/-- A map of the form `z ↦ (f₁ z₁, f₂ z₂)` or `z ↦ (f₁ z₂, f₂ z₁)`, with `f₁`, `f₂` surjective
and vanishing at `0`, preserves the direct sum decomposition. -/
theorem archPermutesSummands_of_form (T : ℂ × ℂ → ℂ × ℂ) (f₁ f₂ : ℂ → ℂ)
    (h₁ : Function.Surjective f₁) (h₂ : Function.Surjective f₂) (h₁0 : f₁ 0 = 0)
    (h₂0 : f₂ 0 = 0)
    (hT : (∀ z, T z = (f₁ z.1, f₂ z.2)) ∨ (∀ z, T z = (f₁ z.2, f₂ z.1))) :
    archPermutesSummands T := by
  unfold archPermutesSummands archSummandFst archSummandSnd
  rcases hT with hT | hT
  · left
    constructor
    · ext w
      simp only [Set.mem_image, Set.mem_ofPred_eq]
      constructor
      · rintro ⟨z, hz, rfl⟩; simp [hT, hz, h₂0]
      · intro hw
        obtain ⟨a, ha⟩ := h₁ w.1
        exact ⟨(a, 0), rfl, by rw [hT]; ext <;> simp [ha, h₂0, hw]⟩
    · ext w
      simp only [Set.mem_image, Set.mem_ofPred_eq]
      constructor
      · rintro ⟨z, hz, rfl⟩; simp [hT, hz, h₁0]
      · intro hw
        obtain ⟨a, ha⟩ := h₂ w.2
        exact ⟨(0, a), rfl, by rw [hT]; ext <;> simp [ha, h₁0, hw]⟩
  · right
    constructor
    · ext w
      simp only [Set.mem_image, Set.mem_ofPred_eq]
      constructor
      · rintro ⟨z, hz, rfl⟩; simp [hT, hz, h₁0]
      · intro hw
        obtain ⟨a, ha⟩ := h₂ w.2
        exact ⟨(a, 0), rfl, by rw [hT]; ext <;> simp [ha, h₁0, hw]⟩
    · ext w
      simp only [Set.mem_image, Set.mem_ofPred_eq]
      constructor
      · rintro ⟨z, hz, rfl⟩; simp [hT, hz, h₂0]
      · intro hw
        obtain ⟨a, ha⟩ := h₁ w.1
        exact ⟨(0, a), rfl, by rw [hT]; ext <;> simp [ha, h₂0, hw]⟩

/-! ## The Chinese remainder isomorphism `ℂ ⊗_ℝ ℂ ≅ ℂ ⊕ ℂ` -/

/-- The `ℝ`-algebra map `ℂ ⊗_ℝ ℂ → ℂ ⊕ ℂ`, `a ⊗ b ↦ (a·b, a·b̄)`. -/
noncomputable def archCrtAlgHom : TensorProduct ℝ ℂ ℂ →ₐ[ℝ] ℂ × ℂ :=
  Algebra.TensorProduct.productMap ((AlgHom.id ℝ ℂ).prod (AlgHom.id ℝ ℂ))
    ((AlgHom.id ℝ ℂ).prod (conjAe : ℂ →ₐ[ℝ] ℂ))

@[simp] theorem archCrtAlgHom_tmul (a b : ℂ) :
    archCrtAlgHom (a ⊗ₜ[ℝ] b) = (a * b, a * conj b) := by
  simp [archCrtAlgHom, Algebra.TensorProduct.productMap_apply_tmul]

theorem archCrtAlgHom_surjective : Function.Surjective archCrtAlgHom := by
  intro z
  refine ⟨((z.1 + z.2) / 2) ⊗ₜ[ℝ] (1 : ℂ) + ((z.1 - z.2) / (2 * I)) ⊗ₜ[ℝ] I, ?_⟩
  rw [map_add, archCrtAlgHom_tmul, archCrtAlgHom_tmul]
  have hI : (I : ℂ) ≠ 0 := I_ne_zero
  ext <;> simp only [map_one, mul_one, conj_I, Prod.mk_add_mk] <;> field_simp <;> ring_nf

theorem archCrtAlgHom_bijective : Function.Bijective archCrtAlgHom := by
  have hdim : Module.finrank ℝ (TensorProduct ℝ ℂ ℂ) = Module.finrank ℝ (ℂ × ℂ) := by
    rw [Module.finrank_tensorProduct, Module.finrank_prod, Complex.finrank_real_complex]
  have hs : Function.Surjective archCrtAlgHom.toLinearMap := archCrtAlgHom_surjective
  exact ⟨(LinearMap.injective_iff_surjective_of_finrank_eq_finrank hdim).mpr hs,
    archCrtAlgHom_surjective⟩

/-- The isomorphism of `ℝ`-algebras `ℂ ⊗_ℝ ℂ ≅ ℂ ⊕ ℂ`, `a ⊗ b ↦ (a·b, a·b̄)`. -/
noncomputable def archCrt : TensorProduct ℝ ℂ ℂ ≃ₐ[ℝ] ℂ × ℂ :=
  AlgEquiv.ofBijective archCrtAlgHom archCrtAlgHom_bijective

@[simp] theorem archCrt_tmul (a b : ℂ) : archCrt (a ⊗ₜ[ℝ] b) = (a * b, a * conj b) := by
  simp [archCrt]

/-- `archCrt` is continuous for the topology of the tensor product metric, so it is an
isomorphism of topological rings. -/
theorem archCrt_continuous : Continuous archCrt :=
  LinearMap.continuous_of_finiteDimensional archCrt.toLinearMap

/-- **(i) for `archCrt`.** The direct sum metric of the images is `2` times the tensor product
metric. -/
theorem archCrt_inner (x y : TensorProduct ℝ ℂ ℂ) :
    archDsInner (archCrt x) (archCrt y) = 2 * inner ℝ x y := by
  induction x using TensorProduct.inductionOn with
  | add x x' hx hx' => rw [map_add, archDsInner_add_left, hx, hx', inner_add_left]; ring
  | tmul a b =>
    induction y using TensorProduct.inductionOn with
    | add y y' hy hy' => rw [map_add, archDsInner_add_right, hy, hy', inner_add_right]; ring
    | tmul c d =>
      simp only [archCrt_tmul, archDsInner, TensorProduct.inner_tmul, Complex.inner]
      simp only [mul_re, mul_im, conj_re, conj_im]
      ring

/-! ## Algebra automorphisms of `ℂ ⊕ ℂ` -/

/-- An `ℝ`-algebra automorphism `θ` of `ℂ ⊕ ℂ` is `z ↦ (g₁ z₁, g₂ z₂)` or `z ↦ (g₁ z₂, g₂ z₁)`
for two `ℝ`-algebra endomorphisms `g₁`, `g₂` of `ℂ`. -/
theorem archAut_form (θ : (ℂ × ℂ) ≃ₐ[ℝ] (ℂ × ℂ)) :
    ∃ g₁ g₂ : ℂ →ₐ[ℝ] ℂ,
      (∀ z, θ z = (g₁ z.1, g₂ z.2)) ∨ (∀ z, θ z = (g₁ z.2, g₂ z.1)) := by
  let d : ℂ →ₐ[ℝ] ℂ × ℂ := (AlgHom.id ℝ ℂ).prod (AlgHom.id ℝ ℂ)
  refine ⟨(AlgHom.fst ℝ ℂ ℂ).comp ((θ : (ℂ × ℂ) →ₐ[ℝ] (ℂ × ℂ)).comp d),
    (AlgHom.snd ℝ ℂ ℂ).comp ((θ : (ℂ × ℂ) →ₐ[ℝ] (ℂ × ℂ)).comp d), ?_⟩
  set e : ℂ × ℂ := (1, 0) with he_def
  have hdec : ∀ z : ℂ × ℂ, z = d z.1 * e + d z.2 * (1 - e) := by
    intro z; ext <;> simp [d, e]
  have hθ : ∀ z : ℂ × ℂ, θ z = θ (d z.1) * θ e + θ (d z.2) * (1 - θ e) := by
    intro z; conv_lhs => rw [hdec z]
    rw [map_add, map_mul, map_mul, map_sub, map_one]
  have hidem : θ e * θ e = θ e := by rw [← map_mul]; congr 1; simp [e]
  have h01 : ∀ a : ℂ, a * a = a → a = 0 ∨ a = 1 := by
    intro a ha
    have : a * (a - 1) = 0 := by rw [mul_sub, ha, mul_one, sub_self]
    rcases mul_eq_zero.mp this with h | h
    · exact Or.inl h
    · exact Or.inr (sub_eq_zero.mp h)
  have hne0 : θ e ≠ 0 := by
    intro h; rw [← map_zero θ] at h
    have := θ.injective h; simp [e] at this
  have hne1 : θ e ≠ 1 := by
    intro h; rw [← map_one θ] at h
    have := θ.injective h; simp [e, Prod.ext_iff] at this
  rcases h01 _ (congrArg Prod.fst hidem) with ha | ha <;>
    rcases h01 _ (congrArg Prod.snd hidem) with hb | hb
  · exact absurd (Prod.ext ha hb) hne0
  · right; intro z; rw [hθ z]; ext <;> simp [ha, hb, d]
  · left; intro z; rw [hθ z]; ext <;> simp [ha, hb, d]
  · exact absurd (Prod.ext ha hb) hne1

/-- An `ℝ`-algebra endomorphism of `ℂ` (the identity or complex conjugation) preserves the
standard Hermitian metric. -/
theorem archAlgHom_inner (g : ℂ →ₐ[ℝ] ℂ) (z w : ℂ) : inner ℝ (g z) (g w) = inner ℝ z w := by
  rcases Complex.real_algHom_eq_id_or_conj g with rfl | rfl
  · rfl
  · simp only [Complex.inner]
    show (conj w * conj (conj z)).re = (w * conj z).re
    simp only [conj_conj, mul_re, conj_re, conj_im]; ring

theorem archAlgHom_surjective (g : ℂ →ₐ[ℝ] ℂ) : Function.Surjective g := by
  rcases Complex.real_algHom_eq_id_or_conj g with rfl | rfl
  · exact fun z => ⟨z, rfl⟩
  · exact fun z => ⟨conj z, by simp⟩

/-- An `ℝ`-algebra automorphism of `ℂ ⊕ ℂ` preserves the direct sum metric. -/
theorem archAut_inner (θ : (ℂ × ℂ) ≃ₐ[ℝ] (ℂ × ℂ)) (x y : ℂ × ℂ) :
    archDsInner (θ x) (θ y) = archDsInner x y := by
  obtain ⟨g₁, g₂, h | h⟩ := archAut_form θ
  · simp only [h, archDsInner, archAlgHom_inner]
  · simp only [h, archDsInner, archAlgHom_inner]; ring

/-- An `ℝ`-algebra automorphism of `ℂ ⊕ ℂ` preserves the direct sum decomposition. -/
theorem archAut_permutesSummands (θ : (ℂ × ℂ) ≃ₐ[ℝ] (ℂ × ℂ)) : archPermutesSummands θ := by
  obtain ⟨g₁, g₂, h⟩ := archAut_form θ
  exact archPermutesSummands_of_form θ g₁ g₂ (archAlgHom_surjective g₁)
    (archAlgHom_surjective g₂) (map_zero g₁) (map_zero g₂) h

/-! ## Isomorphisms of topological rings -/

/-- A continuous ring isomorphism `ℂ ⊗_ℝ ℂ ≅ ℂ ⊕ ℂ` is `ℝ`-linear, hence an `ℝ`-algebra
isomorphism. -/
noncomputable def archAlgEquivOfContinuous (φ : TensorProduct ℝ ℂ ℂ ≃+* ℂ × ℂ)
    (hφ : Continuous φ) : TensorProduct ℝ ℂ ℂ ≃ₐ[ℝ] ℂ × ℂ :=
  AlgEquiv.ofRingEquiv (f := φ) (fun r => by
    rw [Algebra.algebraMap_eq_smul_one, Algebra.algebraMap_eq_smul_one, map_real_smul φ hφ,
      map_one])

@[simp] theorem archAlgEquivOfContinuous_apply (φ : TensorProduct ℝ ℂ ℂ ≃+* ℂ × ℂ)
    (hφ : Continuous φ) (x : TensorProduct ℝ ℂ ℂ) : archAlgEquivOfContinuous φ hφ x = φ x :=
  rfl

/-- Every `ℝ`-algebra isomorphism `ℂ ⊗_ℝ ℂ ≅ ℂ ⊕ ℂ` is `archCrt` followed by an `ℝ`-algebra
automorphism of `ℂ ⊕ ℂ`. -/
theorem archAlgEquiv_eq_aut_comp (φ : TensorProduct ℝ ℂ ℂ ≃ₐ[ℝ] ℂ × ℂ) (x) :
    φ x = (archCrt.symm.trans φ) (archCrt x) := by
  simp

/-- **Proposition 1.5 (i)**, metric form. For every isomorphism of topological rings
`φ : ℂ ⊗_ℝ ℂ ≅ ℂ ⊕ ℂ`, the direct sum metric of `φ x`, `φ y` is `2` times the tensor product
metric of `x`, `y`. -/
theorem archProp1_5_i (φ : TensorProduct ℝ ℂ ℂ ≃+* ℂ × ℂ) (hφ : Continuous φ)
    (x y : TensorProduct ℝ ℂ ℂ) : archDsInner (φ x) (φ y) = 2 * inner ℝ x y := by
  have hx := archAlgEquiv_eq_aut_comp (archAlgEquivOfContinuous φ hφ) x
  have hy := archAlgEquiv_eq_aut_comp (archAlgEquivOfContinuous φ hφ) y
  simp only [archAlgEquivOfContinuous_apply] at hx hy
  rw [hx, hy, archAut_inner, archCrt_inner]

/-- **Proposition 1.5 (i)**, bracketed form: lengths differ by the factor `√2`. -/
theorem archProp1_5_i_length (φ : TensorProduct ℝ ℂ ℂ ≃+* ℂ × ℂ) (hφ : Continuous φ)
    (x : TensorProduct ℝ ℂ ℂ) : √(‖(φ x).1‖ ^ 2 + ‖(φ x).2‖ ^ 2) = √2 * ‖x‖ := by
  rw [← archDsInner_self, archProp1_5_i φ hφ,
    show inner ℝ x x = ‖x‖ ^ 2 from real_inner_self_eq_norm_sq x, Real.sqrt_mul
    (by norm_num), Real.sqrt_sq (norm_nonneg _)]

/-! ## The primitive automorphisms of `ℂ` -/

/-- `archConjIf s` is the identity of `ℂ` for `s = false` and complex conjugation for
`s = true`. -/
def archConjIf (s : Bool) (z : ℂ) : ℂ := if s then conj z else z

theorem archConjIf_mul (s : Bool) (a b : ℂ) :
    archConjIf s (a * b) = archConjIf s a * archConjIf s b := by
  cases s <;> simp [archConjIf]

theorem archConjIf_add (s : Bool) (a b : ℂ) :
    archConjIf s (a + b) = archConjIf s a + archConjIf s b := by
  cases s <;> simp [archConjIf]

theorem archConjIf_pow (s : Bool) (a : ℂ) (n : ℕ) : archConjIf s (a ^ n) = archConjIf s a ^ n := by
  cases s <;> simp [archConjIf]

theorem archConjIf_inv (s : Bool) (a : ℂ) : archConjIf s a⁻¹ = (archConjIf s a)⁻¹ := by
  cases s <;> simp [archConjIf]

theorem archConjIf_conjIf (s t : Bool) (z : ℂ) :
    archConjIf s (archConjIf t z) = archConjIf (xor s t) z := by
  cases s <;> cases t <;> simp [archConjIf]

theorem archConjIf_invol (s : Bool) (z : ℂ) : archConjIf s (archConjIf s z) = z := by
  cases s <;> simp [archConjIf]

/-- The generators named on page 14: complex conjugation and multiplication by `±1` or
`±√−1`, as automorphisms of the metrized real vector space `ℂ`. -/
def archPrimitiveGenerators : Set (ℂ ≃ₗᵢ[ℝ] ℂ) :=
  {f | f = Complex.conjLIE ∨ ∃ u : ℂ, (u = 1 ∨ u = -1 ∨ u = I ∨ u = -I) ∧ ∀ z, f z = u * z}

/-- The **primitive automorphisms** of `ℂ` (page 14): the subgroup of the group of
automorphisms of the metrized real vector space `ℂ` generated by complex conjugation and
multiplication by `±1` or `±√−1`. -/
noncomputable def archPrimitive : Subgroup (ℂ ≃ₗᵢ[ℝ] ℂ) := Subgroup.closure archPrimitiveGenerators

theorem archI_pow_four : I ^ 4 = 1 := by
  rw [show (4 : ℕ) = 2 * 2 from rfl, pow_mul, I_sq]; norm_num

/-- Every primitive automorphism is `z ↦ u · z` or `z ↦ u · z̄` with `u ^ 4 = 1`. -/
theorem archPrimitive_form {f : ℂ ≃ₗᵢ[ℝ] ℂ} (hf : f ∈ archPrimitive) :
    ∃ u : ℂ, u ^ 4 = 1 ∧ ∃ s : Bool, ∀ z, f z = u * archConjIf s z := by
  induction hf using Subgroup.closure_induction with
  | mem f hf =>
    rcases hf with rfl | ⟨u, hu, hfu⟩
    · exact ⟨1, by norm_num, true, fun z => by simp [archConjIf, Complex.conjLIE_apply]⟩
    · refine ⟨u, ?_, false, fun z => by simp [archConjIf, hfu]⟩
      rcases hu with rfl | rfl | rfl | rfl
      · norm_num
      · norm_num
      · exact archI_pow_four
      · rw [neg_pow, archI_pow_four]; norm_num
  | one => exact ⟨1, by norm_num, false, fun z => by simp [archConjIf]⟩
  | mul f g _ _ hf hg =>
    obtain ⟨u, hu, s, hfs⟩ := hf
    obtain ⟨v, hv, t, hgt⟩ := hg
    refine ⟨u * archConjIf s v, ?_, xor s t, fun z => ?_⟩
    · rw [mul_pow, ← archConjIf_pow, hv, hu]; cases s <;> simp [archConjIf]
    · rw [LinearIsometryEquiv.coe_mul, Function.comp_apply, hgt, hfs, archConjIf_mul,
        archConjIf_conjIf, mul_assoc]
  | inv f _ hf =>
    obtain ⟨u, hu, s, hfs⟩ := hf
    have hu0 : u ≠ 0 := by rintro rfl; norm_num at hu
    refine ⟨archConjIf s u⁻¹, ?_, s, fun z => ?_⟩
    · rw [← archConjIf_pow, inv_pow, hu, inv_one]; cases s <;> simp [archConjIf]
    · have hz : f (f⁻¹ z) = z := f.apply_symm_apply z
      rw [hfs] at hz
      have hc : archConjIf s (f⁻¹ z) = u⁻¹ * z := (eq_inv_mul_iff_mul_eq₀ hu0).mpr hz
      calc f⁻¹ z = archConjIf s (archConjIf s (f⁻¹ z)) := (archConjIf_invol _ _).symm
        _ = archConjIf s u⁻¹ * archConjIf s z := by rw [hc, archConjIf_mul]

/-! ## The group of primitive automorphisms has order `8` -/

/-- The four values `1, -1, √−1, -√−1`. -/
noncomputable def archUnit4 : Fin 4 → ℂ := ![1, -1, I, -I]

theorem archUnit4_norm (k : Fin 4) : ‖archUnit4 k‖ = 1 := by
  fin_cases k <;> simp [archUnit4]

theorem archUnit4_injective : Function.Injective archUnit4 := by
  intro k k' h
  fin_cases k <;> fin_cases k' <;> simp [archUnit4, Complex.ext_iff] at h ⊢ <;> norm_num at h

/-- The roots of `u ^ 4 = 1` in `ℂ` are `±1`, `±√−1`. -/
theorem archPow4_eq_one {u : ℂ} (hu : u ^ 4 = 1) : ∃ k, archUnit4 k = u := by
  have h : (u - 1) * (u + 1) * (u - I) * (u + I) = 0 := by
    linear_combination hu + (1 - u ^ 2) * I_sq
  rcases mul_eq_zero.mp h with h | h
  · rcases mul_eq_zero.mp h with h | h
    · rcases mul_eq_zero.mp h with h | h
      · exact ⟨0, by simp [archUnit4]; linear_combination -h⟩
      · exact ⟨1, by simp [archUnit4]; linear_combination -h⟩
    · exact ⟨2, by simp [archUnit4]; linear_combination -h⟩
  · exact ⟨3, by simp [archUnit4]; linear_combination -h⟩

/-- The automorphism `z ↦ u · c_s z` of the metrized real vector space `ℂ`, for `‖u‖ = 1`. -/
noncomputable def archPrimElem (u : ℂ) (hu : ‖u‖ = 1) (s : Bool) : ℂ ≃ₗᵢ[ℝ] ℂ :=
  rotation (⟨u, mem_sphere_zero_iff_norm.2 hu⟩ : Circle) *
    (if s then Complex.conjLIE else 1)

theorem archPrimElem_apply (u : ℂ) (hu : ‖u‖ = 1) (s : Bool) (z : ℂ) :
    archPrimElem u hu s z = u * archConjIf s z := by
  cases s <;> simp [archPrimElem, archConjIf, Complex.conjLIE_apply] <;> exact rotation_apply _ _

theorem archPrimElem_mem (k : Fin 4) (s : Bool) :
    archPrimElem (archUnit4 k) (archUnit4_norm k) s ∈ archPrimitive := by
  have hrot : rotation (⟨archUnit4 k, mem_sphere_zero_iff_norm.2 (archUnit4_norm k)⟩ : Circle)
      ∈ archPrimitive := by
    refine Subgroup.subset_closure (Or.inr ⟨archUnit4 k, ?_, fun z => rotation_apply _ z⟩)
    fin_cases k <;> simp [archUnit4]
  have hc : (if s then Complex.conjLIE else 1) ∈ archPrimitive := by
    cases s
    · exact Subgroup.one_mem _
    · exact Subgroup.subset_closure (Or.inl rfl)
  exact Subgroup.mul_mem _ hrot hc

/-- The map `(k, s) ↦ (z ↦ u_k · c_s z)` onto the primitive automorphisms. -/
noncomputable def archPrimIndex (p : Fin 4 × Bool) : archPrimitive :=
  ⟨archPrimElem (archUnit4 p.1) (archUnit4_norm p.1) p.2, archPrimElem_mem p.1 p.2⟩

theorem archPrimIndex_bijective : Function.Bijective archPrimIndex := by
  constructor
  · rintro ⟨k, s⟩ ⟨k', s'⟩ h
    have h' := congrArg (fun f : archPrimitive => (f : ℂ ≃ₗᵢ[ℝ] ℂ)) h
    simp only [archPrimIndex] at h'
    have h1 := congrArg (fun f : ℂ ≃ₗᵢ[ℝ] ℂ => f 1) h'
    have hI := congrArg (fun f : ℂ ≃ₗᵢ[ℝ] ℂ => f I) h'
    simp only [archPrimElem_apply] at h1 hI
    have hk : k = k' :=
      archUnit4_injective (by cases s <;> cases s' <;> simpa [archConjIf] using h1)
    subst hk
    have hu0 : archUnit4 k ≠ 0 := by
      intro h0; have := archUnit4_norm k; rw [h0, norm_zero] at this; norm_num at this
    have hs : archConjIf s I = archConjIf s' I := mul_left_cancel₀ hu0 hI
    have hs' : s = s' := by
      cases s <;> cases s' <;> simp [archConjIf, Complex.ext_iff] at hs ⊢ <;> norm_num at hs
    rw [hs']
  · rintro ⟨f, hf⟩
    obtain ⟨u, hu, s, hfs⟩ := archPrimitive_form hf
    obtain ⟨k, hk⟩ := archPow4_eq_one hu
    refine ⟨(k, s), Subtype.ext (LinearIsometryEquiv.ext fun z => ?_)⟩
    simp only [archPrimIndex, archPrimElem_apply, hk, hfs]

/-- The group of primitive automorphisms has order `8` (the bracket on page 14). -/
theorem archPrimitive_card : Nat.card archPrimitive = 8 := by
  rw [← Nat.card_congr (Equiv.ofBijective _ archPrimIndex_bijective)]
  simp

/-! ## (ii): the automorphisms of `ℂ ⊕ ℂ` induced by primitive automorphisms -/

/-- The map of `ℂ ⊕ ℂ` that corresponds under `archCrt` to `f ⊗ g`, for `f = u · c_s` and
`g = v · c_t` (`c_s = archConjIf s`). -/
noncomputable def archInducedForm (u v : ℂ) (s t : Bool) (z : ℂ × ℂ) : ℂ × ℂ :=
  if xor s t then (u * v * archConjIf s z.2, u * conj v * archConjIf s z.1)
  else (u * v * archConjIf s z.1, u * conj v * archConjIf s z.2)

theorem archInducedForm_zero (u v : ℂ) (s t : Bool) : archInducedForm u v s t 0 = 0 := by
  cases s <;> cases t <;> simp [archInducedForm, archConjIf]

theorem archInducedForm_add (u v : ℂ) (s t : Bool) (z w : ℂ × ℂ) :
    archInducedForm u v s t (z + w) = archInducedForm u v s t z + archInducedForm u v s t w := by
  cases s <;> cases t <;> refine Prod.ext ?_ ?_ <;>
    simp [archInducedForm, archConjIf] <;> ring

/-- Under `archCrt`, the automorphism `f ⊗ g` of `ℂ ⊗_ℝ ℂ` becomes `archInducedForm`. -/
theorem archInducedForm_crt (f g : ℂ ≃ₗᵢ[ℝ] ℂ) (u v : ℂ) (s t : Bool)
    (hf : ∀ z, f z = u * archConjIf s z) (hg : ∀ z, g z = v * archConjIf t z)
    (x : TensorProduct ℝ ℂ ℂ) :
    archCrt (TensorProduct.congrIsometry f g x) = archInducedForm u v s t (archCrt x) := by
  induction x using TensorProduct.inductionOn with
  | add x y hx hy => rw [map_add, map_add, hx, hy, map_add, archInducedForm_add]
  | tmul a b =>
    simp only [TensorProduct.congrIsometry_apply, TensorProduct.congr_tmul,
      archCrt_tmul]
    change (f a * g b, f a * conj (g b)) = _
    rw [hf, hg]
    cases s <;> cases t <;> refine Prod.ext ?_ ?_ <;>
      simp [archInducedForm, archConjIf] <;> ring

theorem archInducedForm_permutes (u v : ℂ) (s t : Bool) (hu : u ≠ 0) (hv : v ≠ 0) :
    archPermutesSummands (archInducedForm u v s t) := by
  have hcv : conj v ≠ 0 := by rwa [Ne, map_eq_zero]
  have surj : ∀ c : ℂ, c ≠ 0 → Function.Surjective (fun w => c * archConjIf s w) := by
    intro c hc w
    refine ⟨archConjIf s (w / c), ?_⟩
    simp only [archConjIf_invol]; field_simp
  refine archPermutesSummands_of_form _ (fun w => u * v * archConjIf s w)
    (fun w => u * conj v * archConjIf s w) (surj _ (mul_ne_zero hu hv))
    (surj _ (mul_ne_zero hu hcv)) (by cases s <;> simp [archConjIf])
    (by cases s <;> simp [archConjIf]) ?_
  cases h : xor s t
  · left; intro z; simp [archInducedForm, h]
  · right; intro z; simp [archInducedForm, h]

@[simp] theorem archAlgEquivOfContinuous_symm_apply (φ : TensorProduct ℝ ℂ ℂ ≃+* ℂ × ℂ)
    (hφ : Continuous φ) (z : ℂ × ℂ) : (archAlgEquivOfContinuous φ hφ).symm z = φ.symm z :=
  rfl

/-- **Proposition 1.5 (ii).** Let `φ : ℂ ⊗_ℝ ℂ ≅ ℂ ⊕ ℂ` be an isomorphism of topological rings
and `f`, `g` primitive automorphisms of the two copies of `ℂ`. The automorphism of `ℂ ⊕ ℂ`
that corresponds under `φ` to the automorphism `f ⊗ g` of `ℂ ⊗_ℝ ℂ` preserves the direct sum
metric and maps each of the two summands onto a summand. -/
theorem archProp1_5_ii (φ : TensorProduct ℝ ℂ ℂ ≃+* ℂ × ℂ) (hφ : Continuous φ)
    (f g : ℂ ≃ₗᵢ[ℝ] ℂ) (hf : f ∈ archPrimitive) (hg : g ∈ archPrimitive) :
    (∀ x y : ℂ × ℂ, archDsInner (φ (TensorProduct.congrIsometry f g (φ.symm x)))
        (φ (TensorProduct.congrIsometry f g (φ.symm y))) = archDsInner x y) ∧
      archPermutesSummands (fun z => φ (TensorProduct.congrIsometry f g (φ.symm z))) := by
  constructor
  · intro x y
    rw [archProp1_5_i φ hφ, LinearIsometryEquiv.inner_map_map, ← archProp1_5_i φ hφ,
      RingEquiv.apply_symm_apply, RingEquiv.apply_symm_apply]
  · set θ := archCrt.symm.trans (archAlgEquivOfContinuous φ hφ) with hθ
    obtain ⟨u, hu, s, hfs⟩ := archPrimitive_form hf
    obtain ⟨v, hv, t, hgt⟩ := archPrimitive_form hg
    have hu0 : u ≠ 0 := by rintro rfl; norm_num at hu
    have hv0 : v ≠ 0 := by rintro rfl; norm_num at hv
    have hfun : (fun z => φ (TensorProduct.congrIsometry f g (φ.symm z))) =
        θ ∘ archInducedForm u v s t ∘ θ.symm := by
      funext z
      have h1 : θ.symm z = archCrt (φ.symm z) := by simp [hθ]
      have h2 : ∀ w, φ w = θ (archCrt w) := fun w => by simp [hθ]
      simp only [Function.comp_apply]
      rw [h2, h1, ← archInducedForm_crt f g u v s t hfs hgt]
    rw [hfun]
    exact archPermutesSummands_comp (archAut_permutesSummands θ)
      (archPermutesSummands_comp (archInducedForm_permutes u v s t hu0 hv0)
        (archAut_permutesSummands θ.symm))

end IUT.PaperIV.Proposition1_5
